    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S1169A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to mandatory\nseat belt use\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nThis legislation would extend the mandated use of a restraint in the\nback seat of a motor vehicle to the age of eighteen, in turn\nsafeguarding a particularly vulnerable segment of the passenger\npopulation.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe use of seatbelts has proven to mitigate the occurrences of death\nand severe injury caused during motor vehicle accidents. This\nlegislation is simply extending the mandatory use of restraints in the\nback seat in hopes of further reducing fatalities and severe injuries.\nAdditionally, habitual use of safety belts as young adults may\ntranslate to increased use as adults.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection 1: Subdivision 3 of section 1229-c of the vehicle an traffic\nlaw, as added by chapter 365 of the laws of 1984, is amended to\nrequire the use of seatbelts by all individuals under the age of\neighteen in the back seat of a motor vehicle.\n\nSection 2. Effective Date\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n2002 (A.11063-A/S.6302-A)\n2003-04 (A.903/S.118)\n2005-2006 (A.2157-A/S.3582-A)\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone known.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThe act shall take effect on the first of November next succeeding the\ndate on which it shall have become a law.\n",
